{"body":"## Why\n\nThe `Mutation testing` job has failed on every push to `main` since #56 landed (runs [36142775783](https://github.com/k-kinzal/peq/actions/runs/36142775783) and [36148940638](https://github.com/k-kinzal/peq/actions/runs/36148940638)). Its last step rejects a whole-tree run that skipped any mutant, and Infection reported 690 skipped mutants, then 710.\n\nAll of them sit in the eight classes `PhpDocCallDifferenceTest` declared with `#[CoversClass]`. In the two failed reports those files are all but absent (`DocBlock`, `DocContext`, `CallEnrichment`: no mutants at all; `DocIndex`: 1), while their neighbours `DocScope` and `DocVisitor` are reported in full.\n\nInfection charges a mutant the whole run time of every test class that covers it (`TestTotalTimeCalculator` over the JUnit `<testsuite>` time) and skips the mutant without running it when that exceeds the 30-second timeout. `PhpDocCallDifferenceTest` runs a PHPStan analysis in a separate process for each of its 71 cases:\n\n| Class | Tests | Time (no coverage driver) |\n|---|---|---|\n| `PhpDocCallDifferenceTest` | 71 | 182 s |\n\nSo every mutant it reached was skipped rather than tested. The PR-time job runs on changed lines only and does not reject skips, which is why #56 passed its own checks.\n\n## What\n\n- `PhpDocCallDifferenceTest` now covers nothing, as its three siblings under `tests/Diff` already do. The unit tests of `DocBlock`, `DocContext`, `DocExpression`, `DocIndex`, `ReceiverBinding`, `BodyCallRecorder`, `CallSources` and `CallEnrichment` are their covering tests. The test itself is unchanged: it still asserts the call targets and the equality of both engines' graphs.\n- `AGENTS.md` records why a test under `tests/Diff` must not declare coverage.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `composer test:diff`: 262 tests pass.\n- Infection 0.35.4 over the eight files, on whole-suite coverage, with the same options as CI's whole-tree step:\n\n| Total | Killed | Escaped | Skipped | Not covered |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 759 | 591 | 168 | 0 | 0 |\n\n  The 168 escaped mutants were skipped before this change, so they were not being tested either; the whole-tree MSI stays around 90 %, against the required 80 %.\n- `composer lint`: clean.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","title":"Stop the PHPDoc call diff test from claiming coverage"}
